; Property tests (M2.J).
;
; Native only, and deliberately outside the three-runtime gate: the evidence
; that native, js_of_ocaml and Melange agree byte for byte rests on the cram
; baselines, which are the same input on all three. A randomized test is the
; same *distribution* on all three, which is not the same claim, so running it
; three times would cost three times as much and prove nothing extra.
;
; Every run uses a fixed seed. A property test that cannot be reproduced from
; its own transcript reports a failure nobody can act on, and the seed is
; printed with the summary so a CI log is enough to re-run it.
;
; qcheck-core rather than qcheck: no unix, no C stubs, so the linux/i386 and
; linux/arm/v7 CI legs build it like any other pure OCaml library.

; An executable plus a rule rather than a (test) stanza: (test) puts its
; executable in the directory's @all alias whatever its enabled_if says, so
; under ASM_MELANGE=true it would still try to link codec_corpus - which that
; same opt-in has disabled.

(executable
 (name test_props)
 (modes exe)
 (libraries
  qcheck-core
  qcheck-core.runner
  codec
  codec_corpus
  asm_core
  image
  driver
  foundation
  fmt)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (run ./test_props.exe))
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
